## Logging

The application uses two types of logs:

### Access Logs (`logs/access.log`)
Contains detailed information about all requests including:
- Timestamp
- Client IP
- Request method and URL
- Status code
- Query parameters
- Request body (for POST requests)
- User agent
- Referer
- Cookies
- Headers
- Geolocation (if available)

### Debug Logs (`logs/debug.log`)
Contains application debug information including:
- API calls
- Configuration details
- Error details
- Processing status
- Performance metrics

### Log Configuration

Logs are stored in the `logs` directory:
- Files are not executable (chmod 644)
- Maximum file size: 5MB
- Keeps last 5 files for each log type
- Automatically rotates when size limit is reached

### Viewing Logs

1. Access logs:
```bash
tail -f logs/access.log
```

2. Debug logs:
```bash
tail -f logs/debug.log
```

3. In development mode, logs are also printed to the console.

### Log Levels

- ACCESS: Always logged
- DEBUG: Only when ENABLE_DEBUG=true
